window.I18N_LANG="en";window.I18N_ROOT="../";window.I18N_UI=Object.assign(window.I18N_UI||{},{"🔎 전체": "🔎 All", "📌 기타": "📌 Other", "이 묶음에는 없어요 🙈": "Not in this group 🙈", "다른 묶음에 {n}가 있어요.": "There are {n} in other groups.", "개": "", "전체에서 보기": "See all", "\"{q}\"에 대한 검색 결과가 없습니다.": "No results for \"{q}\".", "다른 키워드로 검색하거나, 아래 톡톡으로 문의해 주세요.": "Try other words, or ask us on TalkTalk below.", "이 묶음에는 아직 질문이 없어요.": "There are no questions in this group yet.", "{n}의 질문을 찾았습니다.": "Found {n} questions.", "🔗 이 질문 링크 복사": "🔗 Copy link to this question", "✓ 복사됐어요": "✓ Copied", "주소": "Link", "FAQ가 없습니다.": "No FAQs.", "FAQ를 불러오지 못했습니다.": "Couldn't load the FAQs.", "설명 그림": "Explanation picture", "렌즈 모양 아이콘": "Lens icon", "(한국어)": "(Korean only — translation coming soon)"});window.I18N_PIN={"refund": 70};window.I18N_FAQ={"items": {"4": {"h": "1m1j26u", "q": "The printer machine broke while I was using it.", "a": "📞 Please contact us at the phone number posted in the store, or on Naver TalkTalk.\n\n⏰ Phone: weekdays (Mon–Fri) 9 AM–9 PM\n🚫 No phone support on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.\n💬 At other times and on weekends/holidays: send these 4 things on Naver TalkTalk.\n1. Store name (written on the PC desktop or the sign next to the PC)\n2. Printer machine number\n3. What's wrong\n4. Your contact number\nWe'll contact you after checking.\n\n🙋 If you contacted us but got no answer, file a refund with the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the PC desktop and come back another day.\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n\n⚠️ Even if nothing prints after you pay, NEVER pay again!\nBig files can take more than 10 minutes to print. If your first print comes out while you are paying again, there is no refund. Always contact us first."}, "15": {"h": "17jtcl9", "q": "I paid, but nothing is printing.", "a": "⛔ Don't pay for the same file again!\n\n1. ⏳ Wait about 10 minutes.\n2. 📞 If nothing after 10 minutes, send the store name and the problem on Naver TalkTalk. (Phone is only answered weekdays 9 AM–9 PM)\n   e.g.) \"Gwanggyo store, machine 1: I paid but nothing printed after 10 minutes\"\nA manager will contact you after checking.\n\n🐢 Why is it slow?\n- The file is big.\n- The printer machine is slow.\n- The store internet slowed down for a moment.\n\n🚀 How to print faster (stores have 2 or 3 PCs)\n- Stores with 2 PCs: if you worked on PC1, pay at machine 2; if on PC2, pay at machine 1.\n- Stores with 3 PCs: if you worked on PC1 or PC2, pay at machine 2; if on PC3, pay at machine 1.\n\n🌙 If you paid when there's no phone support (weekdays 9 PM–9 AM, weekends, holidays) and nothing prints and TalkTalk doesn't answer right away, still don't pay again. File a [환불신청] (Refund request) and a manager will contact you the next day.\n\n⏰ Your print may come out after 10 minutes. Even if you're busy, please wait in the store for 10 minutes.\n\n📝 To file a refund: the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n\n👀 How to tell if it's printing\n- If there is a printer icon at the top of the machine screen, it's getting ready to print.\n- If the light at the bottom center of the screen blinks, it's printing.\n- Please wait at this time.\n\n⚠️ If you leave the store without contacting us, it will be hard to refund you later."}, "2": {"h": "11ozofa", "q": "I sent my file, but I can't see it on the printer machine.", "a": "If you typed your PIN at the printer machine and see '검색된 인쇄 작업이 없습니다' (No print jobs found), read below.\n[[img:images/faq/print-nojob.png]]\n\nLook at the [흑백출력] (B&W) / [컬러출력] (Color) print queue window on the PC.\n👀 If something is still in the list, it's still on its way to the printer machine.\n⚠️ If it stays stuck in the list, you can't find it on the printer machine.\n\nTry this.\n1. ⏳ If the file is big, wait a little.\n2. 🔄 If it still doesn't work, restart the PC and print again.\n3. 🔢 Check that the PIN you typed at the printer machine is the same as the PIN you typed on the PC.\n\n🗑️ Files are deleted automatically 30 minutes after you send them."}, "16": {"h": "5p9ghi", "q": "Paper got jammed while printing or copying.", "a": "⛔ Don't pull out the jammed paper!\nThe toner hasn't set yet and can get on your hands. There are no tissues in the store.\n\n1. Leave the paper as it is, and file a [환불신청] (Refund request) on the PC desktop.\n2. For A4: send the print again from the PC, then pay and print at the other machine.\n3. For B4 or A3: first send the details on Naver TalkTalk, and wait for the manager's answer about whether there is a fix.\n   If the manager answers that there is no fix, we're sorry, but please file a refund and come back the next day.\n\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund."}, "17": {"h": "ziwpmj", "q": "I chose the Color printer, but it came out in black and white.", "a": "🎨 To print in color, always check these 3 things.\n1. On the print screen, choose the printer [컬러출력] (Color).\n2. In the preview, check that every page is in color.\n3. On the price screen at the printer machine, check once more that it says [컬러] (Color).\n\n❌ Cases with no refund\n- You didn't choose the Color printer, but thought it would print in color because the preview was in color.\n- You don't remember whether the preview was in color or black and white.\n- You chose the Color printer, so you thought it would print in color even though the preview was black and white.\n- You checked the preview, but some of the pages came out black and white.\n- You chose the Color printer and checked the preview, but it came out black and white. (You mistook the editing screen for the preview)\n- You chose the B&W printer, but thought it would print in color because the preview was in color. (You also didn't check the price screen)\n\n💸 If you chose the Color printer and it came out black and white\n- We partly cancel the payment: the total minus the black-and-white price.\n- File a refund, and send a photo of the black-and-white print on Naver TalkTalk.\n- You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n- We won't process it if the file was edited or you send a different file.\n- If you don't agree to this and ask for a full refund, there is no refund.\n- If you chose the B&W printer and paid, black and white is expected, so there is no refund.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#ptips|How to check color in the preview]]"}, "18": {"h": "2wl9hc", "q": "My print has lines or smudged colors. Can I get a refund?", "a": "Only these 4 line/color/shape problems are refunded. (For blank prints, paper jams, etc., see those FAQs.)\n\n✅ Refunded\n1. A long white line appears. (left to right, or top to bottom)\n2. Colors are smudged.\n3. A single color comes out like a gradient.\n4. Geometric shapes that have nothing to do with the original are printed all over.\n\n📝 How to get a refund\nLeave the print in the store and file it with the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the PC desktop.\n⚠️ If you don't leave the print, there is no refund.\n⚠️ If you don't file a refund by pressing the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon and filling it in, we can't process a refund.\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n\n❌ Not refunded\n1. It's different from the colors on the PC screen. (darker, duller, light blue looks navy, etc.)\n2. The colors are different every time you copy the same color original.\n   → Even the same original can come out in different colors each time. A color difference from the original is never refunded, for any reason.\n3. You printed the same file many times and the colors are different. (Even the same file can come out in different colors.)\n4. It's a Hangul file and the highlighter color doesn't show. (The Hangul viewer has no highlighter function.)\n5. You copied it, but the original's watermark doesn't show. (Watermarks are faint, so they don't copy.)\n6. You copied a certificate and the gold/silver looks strange. (Shiny colors can't be reproduced and come out dark.)\n7. You copied a paper that was already printed once, and part of it doesn't show.\n   → Don't copy a paper that was printed or copied. It gets faint and doesn't show.\n8. It's a PDF made on an iPad and the color doesn't show.\n   → In Acrobat Reader, the preview with [컬러출력] (Color) doesn't show color. You didn't check the preview, so there is no refund.\n   → For iPad PDFs, drag the file into Edge or Chrome and press [인쇄] (Print). Check in the preview that every page is in color, then print.\n9. It's a PDF made in a web design program like Canva and the color doesn't show.\n   → You didn't check the preview, so there is no refund.\n   → Open it in Edge or Chrome and press [인쇄] (Print). Check in the preview that every page is in color, then print.\n10. Pencil writing comes out faint or doesn't show.\n11. A document made by scanning is blurry, or highlighter/transparent colors don't show.\n12. You printed several copies of the same original and the content position is slightly different. (This happens with machines that feed one sheet at a time)\n13. The paper has tiny dots (specks). (They come from paper-making, so they are not defects)"}, "66": {"h": "1145m9y", "q": "I printed/copied in color, but the colors look different from the screen (original). Is the machine broken?", "a": "Usually the machine is not broken. A monitor makes colors with light (RGB), and a printer makes colors with 4 toner colors (CMYK), so the screen and paper can never be exactly the same.\n\n■ Colors are especially different when\n· Vivid colors like red, blue, purple, green; highlighter colors; gold and silver\n· Even the same file can differ page to page and sheet to sheet (especially PDFs made in web design tools like Canva or Miricanvas, PPT, or iPad notes)\n· When copying: gold/silver foil comes out dark, and highlighter colors come out faint or not at all. Light colors (watermarks) may disappear, and copying a paper that was already printed may leave only the dark colors. Documents with anti-copy patterns, like resident registration copies and certificates, may show a pattern like \"사본\" (Copy).\n· Highlighter in Hangul files does not print in the store's Hangul viewer.\n\n■ Try this\n1. Open the PDF in Chrome or Edge, preview all pages, then print\n2. Bring it as a JPG instead of a PDF and print (text may be slightly less sharp)\n※ These raise the chance of smaller color differences. It won't come out 100% the same.\n\n■ Refund rules for color print problems (no exceptions)\nWe refund only these 3: lines, smudged colors, a single color coming out as a gradient. Any other color difference is not eligible for a refund or reprint.\n\n[[img:images/faq/color-notice-poster2.jpg]]"}, "47": {"h": "1ftdts3", "q": "My print came out blank (empty paper).", "a": "📄 There are usually two reasons for a blank print.\n\n1️⃣ The preview had no content\n- Before printing, always check in the preview that every page has content.\n- If the preview looks white, it prints blank.\n\n2️⃣ You opened and printed it straight from a USB\n- USB files must be saved to the PC, then opened and printed.\n- Compressed files must be unzipped before you open them.\n\n🔁 Try printing again like this\n\n📌 It's a PDF made in a web design tool like Canva or Miricanvas\n1. Open Chrome or Edge and drag the file onto that window. (Or right-click the file and choose Edge/Chrome in [연결 프로그램] (Open with).)\n2. Press [인쇄] (Print).\n3. Check in the preview that every page has content.\n4. If all the content shows, print.\n\n📌 It's a PDF but you don't know where it was made\n1. Open Chrome or Edge and drag the file onto that window, or right-click the file and choose Edge/Chrome in [연결 프로그램] (Open with). This fixes most problems with strange colors or blank prints.\n2. Check in the preview that every page has content.\n3. If all the content shows, print again.\n\n💸 File a refund for the blank paper\n1. If you take the blank paper with you or don't leave it where we ask, you may not get a refund. We need to check it really came out blank.\n2. Put the blank paper neatly where the paper is stacked.\n3. Press the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop and file a refund.\n4. A manager checks it, processes it if it's eligible, and tells you the result at the phone number you wrote in the refund request.\n\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you didn't file, or filed after 7 days, there is no refund.\nℹ️ Filing doesn't mean an instant refund. A manager checks it and processes only eligible cases.\n\n📖 To see how to open it in Chrome/Edge and check the preview, tap here.\n[[go:guide-print.html#browser|How to print in Chrome · Edge]]"}, "69": {"h": "1jg5hbw", "q": "My copy came out blank (empty paper).", "a": "🔄 If the original is put in the wrong way, it can come out blank.\n\n📌 The ADF (automatic document feeder) is the 'place to put originals' on top of the printer machine.\n[[sm:images/common/adf-feeder.jpg]]\nThere are two places to put originals, and each one needs a different direction.\n\n📄 1. When putting it in the ADF (top of the machine)\n→ Put it in with the content facing up.\n\n📘 2. When putting it on the glass\n→ Open the top cover of the printer machine.\n→ Put the original with the content facing down toward the glass. (Opposite of the ADF!)\n\n⚠️ If it came out blank because you put it in wrong, you may not get a refund.\n\n✅ If you put it in correctly and it still came out blank, the machine may have a problem. Please file a refund.\nA manager checks it, processes only the eligible cases, and tells you the result at the contact you gave.\nFiling doesn't mean an instant refund.\n⏰ You must file within 7 days of the problem.\n\n👇 File a refund with the picture below.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-refund2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/refund|Go to refund request]]\n💻 There is also a [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop. You can file there too.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-copy.html#adf|How to use the document feeder (ADF)]]\n[[go:guide-copy.html#glass|How to put originals on the glass]]"}, "48": {"h": "1bwd6hc", "q": "The printer machine shows a message like 'No matching paper in the tray'.", "a": "This message can appear even when the machine has paper. You need to fix the print settings and send it again.\n\n🔎 Check first\nIn the machine's list, does [크기] (Size) say 'Custom' or 'Letter' instead of A4·B4·A3?\n\n🛠️ How to fix it\n- PDF: in the print settings, uncheck 'PDF 페이지 크기에 따라 용지 소스 선택' (choose paper source by PDF page size). Then set the paper size you want.\n- Hangul, Word, etc.: [인쇄] (Print) → [컬러출력] (Color) or [흑백출력] (B&W) → [속성] (Properties) → in the [용지] (Paper) tab, set both 'original size' and 'output size' to the same size (e.g. A4).\n\n⛔ Don't change the paper type (heavy paper, premium paper, colored paper, etc.) in the print settings.\nIf you do, a message like 'Load paper in the multipurpose tray' appears and it won't print.\n\n🖼️ Don't select many photos (images) and print them with right-click.\nSave them to the PC, then open them one at a time in [알씨] (ALSee) and print.\n\n🔁 If it was printing fine and this message appeared in the middle, see the FAQ below.\n👉 \"I paid and it was printing fine, then it suddenly said 'no paper' and stopped printing.\"\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#acrobat|PDF print settings]]\n[[go:guide-print.html#hancom|Hangul print settings]]\n[[go:guide-print.html#office|Word · Excel · PowerPoint print settings]]"}, "49": {"h": "1tvh6zb", "q": "My card payment doesn't work.", "a": "1. 💳 Turn the card around so the IC chip side goes in, and insert it again.\n2. 💳 Try another card.\n3. 🖨️ Look up your PIN again at the other printer machine and pay there.\n\n📱 For Samsung Pay, just hold it to the card reader.\nIf it still doesn't work, tell us on TalkTalk. (Phone also works weekdays 9 AM–9 PM) (store name, machine number)"}, "50": {"h": "k6st6p", "q": "The PC screen is black or the mouse doesn't move.", "a": "😊 Don't worry. Follow these steps.\n\n1. 🔘 Hold down the PC power button. Keep holding until the screen turns off completely.\n2. When the screen is fully off and you can't see the mouse pointer, it has shut down.\n3. ⏳ Leave it for a moment.\n4. Press the power button just once to turn it back on.\n5. Wait until the desktop appears.\n\n💡 If the screen doesn't come on, hold the power button again to turn it off completely, then press it once to turn it on.\n🖥️ If it's the same after restarting, please use another PC.\n\n📞 And tell us on TalkTalk. A manager checks the PC remotely.\n- What to send: store name, PC number (e.g. Gwanggyo store, PC 2)"}, "51": {"h": "nco5pa", "q": "The black laminator won't turn on.", "a": "⚫ The black laminator (PL-1506) normally has a blinking red light at 'POWER'.\n\n1. If the red light isn't blinking, there is no power at all. Push the power switch on the back right side of the laminator sideways to connect the power.\n2. If the POWER light is on, press the [전원] (Power) button → the [문서] (Document) button.\n3. When the green light at 'READY' blinks and then stops after about 1 minute, warm-up is done.\n4. Put your print inside the pouch, and slowly feed it into the slot, sealed end first.\n\n⚠️ Putting in only an empty pouch, or only paper without a pouch, can break the machine. Please follow the guide.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-coat.html#pl1506|How to use the black laminator (PL-1506)]]"}, "52": {"h": "15cuo1n", "q": "I don't think the laminating worked well.", "a": "💡 If something seems wrong, tell us first!\n\n1. If you warmed it up and laminated but it doesn't seem to have worked well, don't keep laminating other things.\n2. Send the store name and \"I warmed it up but the laminating doesn't seem to have worked\" on Naver TalkTalk.\n3. If you describe the problem in detail, we can find the cause and tell you how to fix it faster.\n4. A manager checks the TalkTalk message and answers you.\n\n💡 If you kept laminating without noticing, we can only check the first one. So please tell us right away.\nℹ️ Laminating and binding are self-service. If you couldn't do it because the machine broke, we refund the unused pouches and binding covers.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-coat.html#coat|How to laminate]]"}, "53": {"h": "dbzc5q", "q": "The pages of my heat-bound book are falling out.", "a": "It's usually one of these reasons. These cases are not refunded.\n- The pages didn't touch the white glue inside the cover evenly.\n- You didn't push the cover all the way into the binder.\n- You opened it without cooling it for 10+ minutes after taking it out. (If you open it before the glue hardens, pages fall out)\n\n✅ The right order\nWarm up (about 3 minutes, beep) → put the pages neatly in the cover → push it all the way in → press the timer (about 1 minute) → when the light stops, take it out carefully → cool for 10+ minutes → open\n\n🤔 If you don't agree, please file a refund. A manager checks it and tells you separately whether it will be refunded.\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n💡 If binding failed because the machine broke, only the binding covers you paid for are refunded.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-bind.html#bind|How to use heat binding]]"}, "11": {"h": "wf4g01", "q": "I set it to color, but some middle pages came out black and white.", "a": "This happens with PDFs made in places like Canva.\n\n👉 Try opening it in Chrome or Edge and printing.\n1) First open Chrome or Edge, then drag the file onto that window.\n2) Or right-click the file and choose Edge/Chrome in [연결 프로그램] (Open with).\n👀 Before printing, check in the preview that every page is in color.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#browser|How to print in Chrome · Edge]]"}, "8": {"h": "vgbuap", "q": "I pressed [인쇄] (Print) on the machine and it shows [PC]. Should I press it?", "a": "✅ Yes, you're on the right track!\nIt means the file to print is on the PC.\n👉 Press the round [PC] button.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#mfp|How to print at the printer machine]]"}, "22": {"h": "4zt91d", "q": "I want to print a file on my phone.", "a": "📱 Get your phone files by logging in to KakaoTalk for PC with a QR code.\n📧 You can also send it by email. But we can't teach you in the store how to send email from your phone. Please learn it before you come.\n\n📲 How to log in to KakaoTalk for PC with a QR code\n1. Open KakaoTalk on the store PC and press the [QR코드 로그인] (QR code login) button.\n[[img:images/print/kakao-qr-1.png]]\n2. A QR code appears on the PC screen. Scan it with your phone before time runs out.\n[[img:images/print/kakao-pc-qr.png]]\n3. Open KakaoTalk on your phone and press [···(더보기)] (More) at the bottom right. (Most important!) Press the lens icon [[ico:images/print/kakao-lens.png]] at the top, then scan the QR code on the PC screen.\n[[img:images/print/kakao-phone-scan4.png]]\n4. When the 'QR code login' screen appears on your phone, press [1회용 인증하기] (One-time verify).\n[[img:images/print/kakao-once.png]]\n5. A 4-digit number (verification code) appears in the 'Security verification' window on the PC. Type those 4 digits on the phone's 'Security verification' screen and press [확인] (OK). Then KakaoTalk on the PC logs in.\n[[img:images/print/kakao-auth.png]]\n6. Save the file you sent to 'Chat with myself' on your phone to the PC, then open it and print.\n\n⚠️ When you're done, always [로그아웃] (Log out)! Don't check 'auto login'. Your KakaoTalk could be seen by the next customer.\n💻 When you're done, please shut down the PC too.\n- It's best to shut down the PC right after using it. If you forget, it shuts down automatically after 10 minutes if no one uses it.\n- If you leave without shutting it down, the next customer can use it right away before it shuts down automatically. Please shut it down before you leave if you can.\n- If you opened important sites or documents with personal information, be sure to shut the PC down properly and check before you leave.\n💡 The QR code disappears after a while. Press the refresh icon at the bottom right to make a new one.\n💡 Menu positions and names may be slightly different depending on your phone's KakaoTalk version.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#store|How to bring a file to the PC and print it]]"}, "5": {"h": "1ijc50i", "q": "Can I print directly from my phone?", "a": "📵 You can't print directly from your phone.\n\n💻 The store PCs have internet. Do this.\n1. First send the phone file by email or KakaoTalk.\n2. Log in on the store PC and download the file.\n3. Print the downloaded file.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#store|How to print from the PC]]"}, "14": {"h": "vko1yv", "q": "Can I use paper I brought myself?", "a": "❌ No. You can only use the paper in the store.\nDifferent paper can smudge colors or jam in the printer machine.\n\n📄 Store paper\n- A4: Double A 75g\n- B4, A3: Hi-Plus 75g\n\n🙏 Paper you bring can jam or break the machine. Please always use the store's paper."}, "3": {"h": "1ipawtz", "q": "Can I print A3 too?", "a": "✅ Yes, every store can print and copy in A4, B4 and A3.\nYeongtong Station store (영통역점)\n🖨️ Machine 1: A4 only\n🖨️ Machine 2: A4, B4, A3\nSeojeongni Station store (서정리역점)\n🖨️ Machine 1: A4, B4, A3\n🖨️ Machine 2: A4 only\nAll other stores\n🖨️ Machine 1: A4, B4\n🖨️ Machine 2: A4, A3"}, "9": {"h": "1i3nrti", "q": "What is the number I type at the printer machine?", "a": "🔢 It's the 4-digit PIN you typed on the PC.\nThe PIN on the PC and the PIN number at the printer machine mean the same thing. It's like a temporary password to find the document you printed from the PC. We suggest using the last 4 digits of your phone number.\n⚠️ Don't use numbers anyone might use, like 1234 or 1111. Other people's documents may show up along with yours.\n\n📜 If you choose the certificate printer ([증명서전용PIN9999]) on the PC\n- No PIN box appears. 9999 is entered automatically and it's sent to the printer machine.\n- At the PIN step on the printer machine, type 9999.\n- Other customers may have used the certificate printer too, so several documents may appear for 9999. Check the time and document name, and pay and print only yours.\n\n📖 Picture guide for printing certificates (TOEIC · TOEIC Speaking)\n[[go:guide-print.html#cert|How to print certificates]]\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#store|How to type the PIN]]"}, "13": {"h": "uo98e4", "q": "How do I use laminating and heat binding?", "a": "There are two kinds of laminators. Check which one your store has first.\n⚫ Black PL-1506 (laminating only)\n⚪ White SAFA-BM100 (laminating · binding in one)\n\n👍 If the store has both, please use the PL-1506 first. It warms up and laminates faster.\n📖 Follow the guide for your laminator in the top menu [사용방법] (How to Use) → [코팅] (Laminate).\n💰 First check how many pouches there are, and pay first.\n\n📚 How to use heat binding\nHeat binding puts your prints in a cover and melts the glue inside the cover with heat to make them into a book. No hole punching or springs. Heat binding is done on the white combination machine (SAFA-BM100).\n1. Choose a heat-binding cover that fits your number of sheets. You can put in only up to the number written on the cover.\n2. Pay for the cover at the Toss kiosk. It's 1,500 won per cover.\n3. Press the power button, then press the heat [온열] button once to warm it up. After about 3 minutes an alarm sounds and the light stops — warm-up is done.\n4. Put the pages neatly so they touch the glue inside the cover, and push the cover, closed end first, deep into the long slot on top.\n5. Press the timer and wait.\n6. When it's done, take it out, cool it for 10+ minutes, then open it.\n⚠️ Too few sheets (e.g. 5 or 10) can't be bound.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-coat.html#coat|How to laminate]]\n[[go:guide-bind.html#bind|How to use heat binding]]"}, "36": {"h": "omo1l6", "q": "I want to copy my ID card.", "a": "🆔 ID cards are copied on the glass.\n⛔ Don't put them in the document feeder (ADF) on top of the printer machine.\n\n1. Put the ID card at the top-left corner of the glass, at the white arrow.\n2. Put it with the ID content facing the glass. (content down)\n3. On the machine screen, choose the [신분증복사] (ID Copy) option inside [복사] (Copy).\n\n⚠️ Only an ID-card-sized area is copied. If the position is even a little off, it comes out cut off.\n📌 There is a [신분증 복사 방법] (How to copy ID) notice on the wall next to the printer machine. Please follow it.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-copy.html#glass|How to copy an ID card, with pictures]]"}, "37": {"h": "6vf7ft", "q": "How do I put in originals for copy · scan · fax?", "a": "📄 Single-sheet originals go in the 'document feeder (ADF)' on top of the printer machine.\n[[sm:images/common/adf-feeder.jpg]]\n- You can put in up to 100 sheets at once.\n- Put them in with the content facing up.\n- A4 with the long edge to the left; B4·A3 with the short edge to the left.\n- Push them all the way in, and hold them straight with the top and bottom paper guides.\n- When you start, the originals should go into the machine and come back out. If they don't go in, cancel and try again.\n\n📘 Put these originals on the glass, one at a time.\n- Books, ID cards, bankbooks, passports\n- Wrinkled paper, paper with notes stuck on, stapled paper\n- On the glass, line it up with the white arrow at the top-left corner.\n- Put it with the content facing the glass. (Opposite of the ADF!)\n\n⚠️ Leave the original orientation option at [세로] (Portrait) and don't change it. If you change it, the content gets cut off.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-copy.html#adf|How to use the document feeder (ADF)]]\n[[go:guide-copy.html#glass|How to put originals on the glass]]"}, "38": {"h": "1221gy4", "q": "When copying/scanning on the glass, it asks 'Scan another page?' (다른 면을 스캔하시겠습니까?).", "a": "This message always appears when you work on the glass.\n\n1. If you have more originals: first change the original on the glass, then press [예] (Yes).\n2. If you have no more originals: press [아니오] (No).\n\n⚠️ If you press [예] (Yes) without changing the original, the same page keeps getting scanned.\n💡 If the extra-scan window doesn't go away, move to the other printer machine and try there. If it still doesn't work, tell us on TalkTalk. (Phone also works weekdays 9 AM–9 PM)\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-copy.html#glass|About the 'Scan another page?' window]]"}, "39": {"h": "1vi9u2c", "q": "Where is my scanned file?", "a": "💻 Scanned files are on the store PC desktop.\n- If you scanned on machine 1: the [1번복합기스캔함] (Machine 1 scan folder) folder\n- If you scanned on machine 2: the [2번복합기스캔함] (Machine 2 scan folder) folder\n\n📁 You can choose PDF or JPG for the file type. (Searchable-text PDFs are not available)\n⏳ Files are deleted 30 minutes after you pay. Move the file somewhere else as soon as it's made.\n🔌 If you have a USB, move it there. If not, send it to your email over the internet.\n💰 Scanning costs 100 won per side, no matter the size or color/B&W.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-scan.html#scan|How to find your scanned file]]"}, "40": {"h": "1kmcgfy", "q": "Is it cheaper to print two-sided?", "a": "❌ Printing two-sided doesn't lower the price. Only the paper comes out two-sided.\n- The payment info screen shows the full number of pages.\n- Two-sided is charged as 2 sides.\n\n⚠️ A file with only 1 page (e.g. a photo/image) can't be printed two-sided even if you increase the copies.\nA file must have 2 or more pages to print two-sided."}, "41": {"h": "1qgyrx8", "q": "How do I print files from a USB or a compressed file?", "a": "📂 Always save the file to the PC first, then open and print it.\n- If you open and print a file directly from the USB, it may come out blank.\n- Unzip compressed files (zip, etc.) before opening and printing them.\n- Saving to the desktop makes it easy to find.\n\n🔍 If you can't find the saved file\n- Files from the internet: [파일 탐색기] (File Explorer) → [다운로드] (Downloads) folder\n- Files from KakaoTalk: [파일 탐색기] (File Explorer) → [문서] (Documents) → [카카오톡] (KakaoTalk) folder\n\n⚠️ Blank or cut-off prints caused by not following the guide are not refunded.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#store|How to save a file to the PC and print it]]"}, "42": {"h": "98zq57", "q": "The payment info screen shows something I didn't want.", "a": "🛑 Don't pay. Just send it again from the PC.\n\n1. Don't pay at the printer machine. Leave it as it is.\n2. Set the print options again on the PC.\n3. Change your PIN to a new number and print again.\n4. Look it up with the new number at the printer machine, then pay.\n\n💡 Unpaid items are deleted automatically after 30 minutes.\n⚠️ If you pay without checking the payment info screen, there is no refund.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#ptips|How to check the payment info screen]]\n[[go:guide-print.html#mfp|How to pay at the printer machine]]"}, "43": {"h": "1bkrf8b", "q": "Several files show up in the printer machine's list. Which one should I choose?", "a": "👀 Choose and pay only for your own documents.\n- Before paying, match the time and file name to make sure the documents in the list are yours.\n- Documents printed because you paid without checking can't be refunded.\n- If you used the certificate printer ([증명서전용PIN9999]), look up 9999 and find your document.\n\n⚠️ Be careful with [모두선택] (Select all)!\nIf you pay for someone else's file along with yours without noticing, there is no refund.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#mfp|How to choose from the list at the printer machine]]"}, "44": {"h": "n6258s", "q": "Can I connect my laptop to the printer machine and print?", "a": "❌ No. You can't connect a personal laptop directly to the printer machine or print over Wi-Fi.\n\n👉 Change your file to PDF, move it by USB, email or KakaoTalk, and print it from the store PC."}, "45": {"h": "poizux", "q": "Can I print with no margins (full bleed)?", "a": "❌ There is a margin of about 5mm on all sides, no matter the paper size.\n\nTo print with no margins, please use a professional print shop. 🙏"}, "46": {"h": "7bu9dc", "q": "How much does it cost?", "a": "💰 Printing · copying (per side)\n- B&W: A4 70 won, B4 120 won, A3 140 won\n- Color: A4 250 won, B4 400 won, A3 500 won\n- Two-sided is charged as 2 sides.\n\n📄 Scanning: 100 won per side (same for any size)\n📠 Fax: 500 won per side (sent in black and white only)\n✨ Laminating: A4 400 won/sheet, A3 800 won/sheet\n📚 Heat binding: 1,500 won per cover (same for any thickness)\n🛍️ Products: L-folders · slide-binder files · document envelopes 600 won each\n\n💡 You can also see the price list in the [서비스] (Services) menu of the website.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:services.html#price|See the price list]]"}, "30": {"h": "1ereuax", "q": "The store has CCTV, right? I want to see the footage.", "a": "✅ You can see footage of the time you were there, after we confirm your identity.\n\n📹 2 ways to see the footage\n1. See it in person\n- Meet a manager, confirm your identity, then watch the footage.\n- You don't choose the date and time yourself; you agree on it with the manager.\n2. Hear it by phone\n- If meeting is hard, after confirming your identity we briefly tell you what's in the footage by phone.\n⚠️ Asking to check footage doesn't mean we check it right away.\n\n💬 How to apply\nSend these 3 things on Naver TalkTalk.\n1. The date and time of the footage you want to check\n2. The last 4 digits of the card you paid with\n3. Why you want to check the footage\nA manager will contact you separately after checking.\n\n👥 What if other people are in the footage?\n- We blur other people so they can't be recognized (de-identification) before showing it.\n- The person who asked for the footage pays the cost of blurring.\n\n⏳ It isn't processed right away\nEven if you ask by phone or TalkTalk, we can't do it right away. It may take a few days for a manager to receive the request and check the footage.\nA manager will contact you separately after checking.\n\n📹 It may be hard to find with footage\n- Footage is kept for 7 days from the time it was recorded. Even within that period, it may not be viewable if there's a problem with the CCTV company's server or viewing equipment.\n- There are blind spots, and things like an ID card left inside the scanner may not be visible."}, "29": {"h": "18dzcsk", "q": "I left my ID card, card or USB behind. Can you keep it for me?", "a": "This is an unmanned store, so it's hard for us to keep items left behind. 🙏\n\n🆔 If you lost an ID card or credit card\n1. First contact the issuer (card company, etc.) to report the loss or suspend it.\n2. Come to the store as soon as possible.\n3. Look around where you sat.\n4. If it isn't there, check the [분실물보관함] (Lost-and-found box) in the store that looks like a mailbox.\n\n📮 How the lost-and-found box is used\n- When customers or managers find an item, they put it in the box.\n- Some customers find items but don't put them in.\n- It does not mean we keep a lost-item log or take responsibility for keeping items.\n- It's a minimum measure to stop others from using ID cards or cards.\n\n🔒 The box is locked with a password\n- How to get the password is on the notice near the box. Follow it.\n- If you lost the card you paid with at the store and don't know the payment details: pay again in the store with another card, and use that payment to get the password.\n- If there's nothing to buy in the store: check the payment details, such as the approval number, with your card company to get the password.\n\n⚠️ Managers do not tell you past payment details by phone.\nThe steps are complicated, so please be careful not to lose your things.\n\n🔒 The lost-and-found box is provided for customers' convenience. We are not responsible for keeping, returning or losing items.\n⛔ Don't use the box to leave your own things, only for items found in the store.\n💍 Don't put valuables like cash or jewelry in it.\n\n🔑 How to get the password\n[[go:faq.html#faq-71|How to use the lost-and-found check site]]\n- Press the [분실물확인] (Lost item check) icon on the store PC desktop.\n- Enter your payment details and phone number, and get the password by text message.\n- Please do it yourself. Managers won't tell you instead.\n- After checking the box, be sure to lock it properly.\n\n👮 If you find out someone took it, report it to the police.\n\n⏳ Items not picked up for a long time may be disposed of.\n\n⚖️ Related law (simple explanation)\n- Lost Articles Act, Article 1: a person who finds an item must return it to the owner or hand it to the police.\n- Civil Act, Article 693: 'keeping' an item only exists when the person leaving it and the person receiving it agree. An unmanned store never agreed to keep customers' items. So it's hard to ask the store manager to find it for you.\n\n🚓 Check with the police too\nFound items are sometimes handed to the police. You can search the National Police Agency's lost-item portal Lost112 (www.lost112.go.kr) or call 182."}, "21": {"h": "2iiqk7", "q": "I was using a site with limited print counts and the PC froze.", "a": "⚠️ If the PC has a problem while you're using the sites below, we can't compensate you.\n- Sites where you get a document after paying\n- Sites with a limited number of prints\n- Sites where you can't save the document you made\n(There's a notice on the store PC too.)\n\n🤔 Why do problems happen?\n- We don't block any particular site.\n- But the security programs those sites install can conflict with the store PC and cause problems.\n\n🔄 When the store PC restarts, all downloaded programs and login info are erased. Be careful with sites that need the PC to be restarted."}, "19": {"h": "u55pi7", "q": "I was trying to print my TOEIC score report and the PC froze.", "a": "📜 When printing certificates from the YBM site (TOEIC · TOEIC Speaking · TOEFL score certificates) or school graduation/transcript sites that use Certpia, always choose the printer [증명서전용PIN9999] (certificate printer).\n(This does not apply to Government24 · Hometax · court sites.)\n\n⚠️ If you choose the Color or B&W printer, the PC freezes, and you may have to pay again to get the certificate.\n\n1. Pay on the site and get the certificate.\n2. When you open the document and print, choose the printer [증명서전용PIN9999].\n3. At the printer machine, look up PIN 9999 and pay, and it prints.\n\n💡 The PIN is the number you typed on the PC. It's like a temporary password for finding the document you sent from the PC at the printer machine.\n\n❌ We don't compensate for money lost because the guide wasn't followed. (There's a notice in the store too.)\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#cert|How to print certificates]]"}, "23": {"h": "dds97b", "q": "My Hangul file's text is broken and the layout is off.", "a": "📄 Hangul on the store PC is a view-only program (viewer).\nIf the store PC doesn't have the fonts of the computer that made the file, text may break, strange symbols may appear, or the layout may get messed up.\n\n👉 Please bring Hangul files converted to PDF.\n\n👀 Before printing, always check for broken text or strange symbols.\n⚠️ We can't take responsibility for wrong prints made without checking.\nProblems from different fonts or program versions can't be fixed in the store.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#hancom|How to print Hangul files]]"}, "20": {"h": "8q81g9", "q": "Documents won't open on the Internet Registry Office, Government24 or court sites.", "a": "Government and financial sites have frequent security updates. So they can conflict with Windows, the browser and other programs on the store PC.\n\n🙏 In this case there is nothing the store can do for you.\n⚠️ We don't compensate for problems that happen while using these sites. (There's a notice on the store PC too.)"}, "10": {"h": "7e89a7", "q": "When I opened my Hangul file, I see unknown symbols (□).", "a": "It's not broken! 👌\nIt happens because the fonts (letter styles) on the computer that made the file are different from the store PC.\n\nIt prints exactly as you see on the screen.\n👉 Please save Hangul files as PDF before you come.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#hancom|How to print Hangul files]]"}, "57": {"h": "1gjckxk", "q": "Can I edit PDF or Hangul files?", "a": "❌ PDF and Hangul (HWP) are view-only programs (viewers), so you can't edit.\n\n💡 For Hangul files, you can make simple edits with the [한글편집(Polaris)] (Hangul editor, Polaris) program on the desktop.\nBut the layout may break depending on the file size or version.\n\n👉 Please edit files at home first and bring them as PDF.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-print.html#hancom|How to print Hangul files]]"}, "58": {"h": "1h21n0d", "q": "Can I print certificates from Government24 or Hometax? What about digital certificates?", "a": "✅ Yes, you can use public sites like Government24 and Hometax. You can use digital certificates too.\n\n🔑 Bring your digital certificate on a USB or move it to the PC. (It's erased when the PC restarts)\n\n⚠️ Government and financial sites have many security programs and can conflict with the store PC. We don't compensate for problems that happen then.\n⚠️ Some certificates may print blank because of file size or format. Always check the preview before printing.\n🆘 We recommend not using documents you have to pay for or documents with a limited number of prints.\n\n🚫 Don't use [증명서전용PIN9999] (certificate printer) for Government24 · Hometax · court (Internet Registry Office) documents.\n💳 What you pay on these sites to issue documents has nothing to do with PrintShop Mini. You pay PrintShop Mini at the printer machine, and the document prints at the end after paying.\n🖨️ Open the document you got from the site on the PC, send the print job, then pay at the printer machine.\n[[go:guide-print.html#store|How to print]]"}, "59": {"h": "iht9xr", "q": "How do I print files from special programs like CAD?", "a": "❌ The store PCs don't have programs like CAD, Photoshop or Illustrator.\n\n👉 Please convert them to PDF at home before you come.\n🖼️ Combining several images into one PDF is hard with the store PC's programs. Use an outside site or make it before you come.\n📂 If you got the PDF as a compressed file, unzip it before printing."}, "24": {"h": "1pfag4s", "q": "I don't have a card. Can I pay with cash or bank transfer? (Toss kiosk prepaid top-up)", "a": "⚠️ If you have an IC card (credit/debit) or Samsung Pay, don't pay at the Toss kiosk!\n💳 At the payment step, insert your IC card into the printer machine's card reader, or hold Samsung Pay to it.\n💸 If you pay by mistake at the Toss kiosk, refunds are returned minus a fee.\n\n❌ Cash and bank transfer are not accepted.\n🧾 No card? No problem! Pay first at the Toss kiosk with Apple Pay · Kakao Pay · Toss Pay · QR easy pay, and use the top-up card.\n\n🎬 Watch the video first\n[[vid:videos/guide-toss.mp4]]\n\n📍 Where is the Toss kiosk?\nIt's on the desk with the white binding·laminating machine (SAFA-BM100). Products like laminating pouches, L-folders and document envelopes are usually on this desk too.\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-where.png]]\n\n🧮 First check the price at the printer machine\n\n🖨️ For printing\n1. 💻 Open the file to print on the PC, and go as far as typing your PIN (4 digits).\n2. At the printer machine, press [인쇄] (Print) → [PC] and type your PIN.\n3. Choose your document and press [시작] (Start), and the price screen appears. Look at B&W/color, pages and price, and remember them.\n\n📋 For copy · scan · fax\n- Read the guide first, and work out the price from how many originals there are and whether it's B&W or color.\n\n🏧 Pay at the Toss kiosk\n1. Go to the Toss kiosk and press [결제하기] (Pay).\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-kiosk.png]]\n2. Press [선불충전] (Prepaid top-up) in the tabs at the top.\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-s1-tab.png]]\n3. Choose exactly what you saw on the printer machine. e.g.) Printing B&W → [복사/인쇄-A4-흑백-1장] (Copy/Print-A4-B&W-1 sheet), Scanning 1 sheet → [스캔-1장] (Scan-1 sheet)\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-s2-item.png]]\n4. When \"안내를 받으셨습니까?\" (Did you receive guidance?) appears, press [예(안내를 받았습니다.)] (Yes). Adjust the number of sheets with [+] [−].\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-s3-agree.png]]\n💡 You have to press [예] (Yes) at \"Did you receive guidance?\" to continue paying.\n💡 But you don't have to call a manager to use the prepaid top-up. If you've read and understood this guide, press [예] (Yes) and continue without calling.\n💡 If you're still not sure, ask a manager by phone or TalkTalk.\n💡 The moment you pay the prepaid top-up, the money is loaded onto the top-up card hanging from the printer machine's card reader.\n5. Press [바로 결제] (Pay now), or if you have more to pay for, press [담기] (Add to cart) and pay from the cart.\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-s4-direct.png]]\n6. When \"이대로 결제할까요?\" (Pay like this?) appears, press [○○원 결제하기] (Pay ○○ won).\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-s5-confirm.png]]\n7. Choose a payment method: [애플·NFC] (Apple·NFC) or [QR 간편결제] (QR easy pay). For apps like Kakao Pay or Naver Pay, press [QR 간편결제] (QR easy pay). (For Samsung Pay, pay directly at the printer machine's card reader)\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-s6-method-v2.png]]\n8. If you pressed [QR 간편결제] (QR easy pay), hold your phone's payment QR code up to the Toss kiosk screen.\n[[img:images/faq/pay-toss-s7-qr.png]]\n💡 For both B&W and color, press [담기] (Add to cart), add one more with [더 담기 +] (Add more +), and pay together.\n\n💳 Tap the top-up card at the printer machine\n1. After paying, go to the printer machine. For copy · scan · fax, put in the originals following the guide, do the job, and press [확인] (OK) on the price screen.\n2. When it says \"카드를 대 주세요\" (Please tap your card), tap the white card hanging on a string from the card reader, like a T-money card.\n[[img:images/faq/pay-card-terminal.png]]\n\n✅ After paying, prints and copies come out, scans become files, and faxes turn the originals into a file and start sending.\n\n⚠️ The price at the printer machine and the amount you paid at the Toss kiosk must be exactly the same.\n⚠️ Money paid at the Toss kiosk stays on the top-up card for only 20 minutes. Don't pay first; check the price at the printer machine, then pay.\n⚠️ Don't pay twice. Double payments are refunded minus a fee.\n💡 Toss kiosk payments are refunded only to a bank account. For details, see 'When and how are refunds processed?'.\n\n📖 Tap to learn how to do the job first.\n[[go:guide-print.html#store|How to print]]\n[[go:guide-copy.html|How to copy]]\n[[go:guide-scan.html|How to scan]]\n[[go:guide-fax.html|How to send a fax]]"}, "67": {"h": "klpm2u", "q": "Can I pay with Kakao Pay or Naver Pay? How?", "a": "✅ You can pay at the Toss kiosk. The card reader next to the printer machine accepts only credit/debit cards and Samsung Pay.\nThe way depends on the service you want to use.\n\n🛍️ When paying for products (laminating pouches · heat-binding covers · L-folders · slide-binder files · document envelopes)\n1. Press [결제하기] (Pay) at the Toss kiosk and choose the product.\n2. For the payment method, press [QR 간편결제] (QR easy pay).\n3. On your phone, open the payment QR code in the Kakao Pay (or Naver Pay) app.\n4. Hold the QR code up to the kiosk screen (the camera at the top).\n5. Wait until the payment is done.\n\n🖨️ For printing · copying · scanning · fax\n- Pay with [선불충전] (Prepaid top-up) at the Toss kiosk.\n- Press [QR 간편결제] (QR easy pay) as the payment method to use Kakao Pay · Naver Pay.\n- There are many steps, so be sure to read the guide with pictures. It's explained in detail in 'FAQ: I don't have a card. Can I pay with cash or bank transfer? (Toss kiosk prepaid top-up)'."}, "31": {"h": "1dwusmx", "q": "How do I get a parking discount (parking registration)?", "a": "🅿️ Apply for a parking discount at '주차등록' (Parking registration).\n\n🚫 Stores with no parking discount\n- Gwonseon store (권선점)\n- Dongbaek Station store (동백역점)\nThese two stores have parking lots, but they are paid.\nPrintShop Mini does not give parking discounts there. 🙏\n\n✅ For other stores, tap the picture below to apply.\n\n📋 Each store has a different parking discount policy!\nWhen you choose your store (branch) on the site, its parking discount policy appears.\nRead the policy carefully before applying for the discount.\n\n👇 The parking registration site opens.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-parking2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/parking|Go to parking registration]]\n💻 There is also a [주차할인] (Parking discount) icon on the store PC desktop. You can apply there too.\n\n📝 Do this\n1. In [지점명] (Store name), choose the store where you parked. Its parking discount info (time, conditions) appears. Please read it carefully.\n2. In [카드 구분] (Card type), choose how you paid.\n   - Samsung Pay · Apple Pay · kiosk payment (binding · laminating): enter the [승인번호(8자리)] (8-digit approval number).\n   - Credit card (physical card): enter the [앞 4자리] (first 4 digits) and [뒤 4자리] (last 4 digits) of the card number.\n3. Enter [차량번호(4자리)] (car number, 4 digits).\n4. Press [검색] (Search). It may take a little while to find your car. Please wait until the screen changes.\n5. Check that your car number, entry time and car photo are correct.\n6. Press [주차할인적용] (Apply parking discount), and when \"주차 할인권을 적용하시겠습니까?\" (Apply the parking discount?) appears, press [주차할인적용] once more.\n7. When \"주차 할인권이 등록되었습니다\" (Parking discount registered) appears, you're done.\n\n🔎 Tap to see how to find the approval number.\n[[go:faq.html#faq-6|How to find the Samsung Pay · Apple Pay approval number]]\n\n⚠️ If you see these screens, do this\n- \"결제 정보를 찾을 수가 없습니다\" (Payment info not found): check the store, card type and card number (approval number) again.\n- \"차량 정보를 찾을 수가 없습니다\" (Car info not found): check the car number again.\n- \"결제하신 금액이 주차 할인을 받기 위한 최소 금액보다 적습니다\" (Amount paid is less than the minimum): check the minimum payment in your store's parking discount info.\n- \"이미 주차 등록된 이력이 존재합니다\" (Already registered): it's already registered with the same payment.\n- \"등록이 실패하였습니다\" (Registration failed): tell us on TalkTalk as shown below.\n\n⚠️ If registration doesn't work on the site, don't drive out — tell us on TalkTalk. (Phone also works weekdays 9 AM–9 PM)\n✉️ What to send on TalkTalk\n1. Store name\n2. Contact number\n3. Last 4 digits of the car number\n4. The problem (parking discount site error)\n⏳ Please wait in the store for a moment while a manager checks. The store isn't responsible for parking fees if you drive out first without contacting us.\n💳 If you paid several times with the same card, you may be able to register them together. (Different cards can't be combined)"}, "6": {"h": "1h6dk6j", "q": "I need a receipt. Can I get one?", "a": "🧾 You can get a receipt at '영수증신청' (Receipt request).\n👇 Tap the picture below to open the receipt request site.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-receipt2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/receipt|Go to receipt request]]\n💻 There is also a [영수증신청] (Receipt request) icon on the store PC desktop. You can apply there too.\n\n📝 Do this\n1. In [지점명] (Store name), choose the store where you paid.\n2. In [결제일자] (Payment date), choose the date you paid.\n3. In [카드 구분] (Card type), choose how you paid.\n   - Samsung Pay · Apple Pay · kiosk payment (binding · laminating): enter the [승인번호(8자리)] (8-digit approval number).\n   - Credit card (physical card): enter the [앞 4자리] (first 4 digits) and [뒤 4자리] (last 4 digits) of the card number.\n4. Press [검색] (Search). When your payments appear, check the one you need a receipt for.\n5. Choose the receipt type you want.\n   - Card receipt (image)\n   - Statement of transaction (PDF)\n6. Enter [고객명] (Customer name) and [고객연락처] (Customer contact). Add [비고] (Notes) if needed.\n7. Press [발급하기] (Issue), and when the window opens, press [다운로드] (Download) to save the file. Please wait a moment while the file is made.\n\n🔎 Where do I find the approval number?\nIf you paid with Samsung Pay, tap the payment in the Samsung Pay app. The 8-digit [승인번호] (approval number) at ③ appears.\n[[img:images/faq/pay-approve-samsung.jpg]]\nIf you paid with Apple Pay, check it in the Hyundai Card app as shown below.\n[[img:images/faq/pay-approve-apple.jpg]]\n\n⚠️ If \"결제 정보를 찾을 수가 없습니다\" (Payment info not found) appears, check the store, payment date and card number (approval number) again and search.\n💡 If you paid several times with the same card, the receipts may come out combined."}, "70": {"h": "17o0xwe", "q": "Refunds at a glance: what is and isn't refunded", "a": "📝 Please know this first\n- For a refund you must file a [환불접수] (Refund request). Without filing, there is no refund.\n- ⏰ You must file within 7 days of the problem. After 7 days, we can't process the refund.\n- Filing doesn't mean an instant refund. A manager checks it, processes only eligible cases, and tells you the result separately at the contact you gave.\n- Leave the problem print in the store when you file. If you don't leave it, there is no refund.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-refund2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/refund|Go to refund request]]\n💻 You can also file with the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop.\n\n✅ Eligible for a refund (processed after a manager checks)\n- Machine breakdown, paper jam, toner smudge\n- Blank pages because the printer machine broke\n- A long white line appears\n- Colors are smudged\n- A single color comes out like a gradient\n- Shapes unrelated to the original are printed all over\n- You paid but nothing printed after more than 10 minutes (don't pay again — contact us first)\n- Pages that didn't print because it stopped with \"no paper\" (only the pages that didn't print)\n- You chose the Color printer but it came out black and white (we partly cancel: the total minus the B&W price)\n- The fax failed ([전송실패], Send failed) because the receiving number was wrong (we cancel the payment)\n- You couldn't laminate or bind because the machine broke (only unused pouches and heat-binding covers are refunded)\n\n❌ Not refunded\n\n📌 You didn't file\n- You didn't file, or 7 days have passed\n- You didn't leave the print\n- You left the store without contacting us\n\n📌 You didn't check before paying\n- You paid without looking at the payment info screen (B&W/color, two-sided/one-sided, paper size, pages, price)\n- You paid without checking it was your document, or paid for other people's files too with [모두선택] (Select all)\n\n📌 You didn't read the guide or check the preview\n- It went wrong because you worked without reading the guide\n- You could see in the preview that content was cut off, but printed anyway\n- You printed without checking color/B&W in the preview (e.g. you chose the Color printer but printed even though the preview was black and white)\n- You printed a USB file without saving it to the PC, and it came out blank\n- You didn't save a compressed file to the PC, unzip it, and open the unzipped file by double-clicking before printing\n- You didn't save a file from email · cloud · web drive to the PC and open the saved file by double-clicking before printing\n\n📌 You put it in or typed it wrong\n- The original was put in wrong, so it came out blank or cut off (copy · scan · fax)\n- You typed the wrong fax number, but it was a working fax number, so it shows [전송완료] (Sent)\n\n📌 The colors are different (a color difference from the original is never refunded, for any reason)\n- It's different from the colors on the PC screen\n- The colors are different every time you copy the same original\n- Gold/silver comes out dark, highlighter colors don't show\n- The watermark doesn't show\n- You copied a paper that was already printed or copied, and part of it doesn't show\n- Pencil writing comes out faint, a scanned document is blurry\n\n📌 Other\n- Highlighter color in a Hangul file doesn't show (the Hangul viewer has no highlighter function)\n- The paper has tiny dots (specks)\n- The pages of a heat-bound book fall out (they didn't touch the glue evenly, weren't pushed all the way in, or you opened it without cooling for 10 minutes)\n\n📌 You paid again or paid twice\n- You paid again because nothing printed, and then your first print came out\n- You sent a fax again without waiting and paid twice\n- You paid twice by mistake at the Toss kiosk (refunded minus a fee)\n\n📌 Certificate · government sites\n- Problems from PC crashes while using sites where you get a document after paying, sites with limited print counts, or government/financial sites\n- The PC crashed because you didn't choose [증명서전용PIN9999] (certificate printer) for TOEIC, school transcripts/graduation certificates or Certpia (the certificate fee is not refunded)\n\n💳 If you paid at the Toss kiosk\n- It can't be cancelled on the card. We refund to a bank account.\n- In the refund request, choose [직접입력] (Enter directly) as the reason, and write the bank name, account number and account holder's name.\n\n👇 If you've read the above, please file a refund.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-refund2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/refund|Go to refund request]]\n💻 You can also file with the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop.\n\n📖 Tap below for more details.\n[[go:faq.html#faq-12|My print came out wrong. Can I get a refund?]]\n[[go:faq.html#faq-54|When and how are refunds processed?]]\n[[go:faq.html#faq-18|My print has lines or smudged colors]]\n[[go:faq.html#faq-17|I chose the Color printer but it came out black and white]]"}, "26": {"h": "3cmfad", "q": "The product I want to buy isn't on display.", "a": "📦 L-folders, document envelopes, slide-binder files, laminating pouches and heat-binding covers can only be paid for and used if they are on display.\n\n🙏 Please don't take out stock stored in the store without a manager's permission.\n\nWhat if the type or amount you want isn't there?\n- Use only what's on display.\n- Please come another day to buy the rest.\n\n🙏 We check the display stock often so you aren't inconvenienced. But it's hard to know when things will sell out, so you may not be able to buy what you want. We appreciate your understanding."}, "27": {"h": "1kil8qq", "q": "I paid at the Toss kiosk. Can I take a different product with the same price?", "a": "🙏 Please take exactly the product you paid for.\n\nL-folders, document envelopes and slide-binder files are currently (as of 2026) the same price: 600 won each. But we need to track stock, so swapping is hard.\ne.g.) If you paid for 1 L-folder (600 won) at Toss, take an L-folder. Please don't take a document envelope or slide-binder file.\n\n🙋 If you really need to swap, tell us on Naver TalkTalk.\n1. Scan the Naver TalkTalk QR posted in the store.\n2. Leave the store name, the product you paid for, and the product you took instead.\nIt helps us a lot with checking stock. 🙏\n\n📅 Prices are scheduled to change from 2027."}, "60": {"h": "1oyfi8h", "q": "I left without paying for a product.", "a": "🙏 Products are taken out after paying. It's okay if you forgot to pay.\n\n👉 If you noticed later, send this on Naver TalkTalk.\n- Store name\n- Contact number\n- The time you used the store\n- The type and number of products you used\nA manager will check and tell you how to pay.\n\n⚠️ Taking products without paying can be a legal problem. Please tell us as soon as you notice.\n💡 First check the products are there, pay first, then take them out."}, "72": {"h": "1wky1tg", "q": "Opening hours and store information (24 hours · phone support · Wi-Fi)", "a": "🏪 This is how PrintShop Mini works.\n\n⏰ Opening hours\n✅ Every store is open 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, with no days off.\n✅ Open on public holidays, Korean holidays, long weekends and temporary holidays too.\n🤖 It's an unmanned store with no staff. Customers do things themselves, and if there's a problem, contact us by phone or TalkTalk.\n\n📞 Phone support hours\n- Phone support is only on weekdays (Mon–Fri) 9 AM–9 PM.\n- The phone number is posted all around the store, such as on the PC desktop and monitors.\n🚫 No phone support on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.\n💬 At other times and on weekends/holidays, please contact us on Naver TalkTalk.\n\n📝 What to send on TalkTalk\n1. Store name (written on the PC desktop or the sign next to the PC)\n2. Printer machine number\n3. The problem\n4. Contact number\nA manager will contact you after checking.\n\n📍 Store location\nSearch '프린트샵미니 + store name' on Naver to see the location, building name, floor and phone number.\n\n🚫 Please follow these rules\n- Pets are not allowed in the store.\n- Food is not allowed in the store either.\nPlease help keep it clean and safe. 🙏\n\n📶 Free Wi-Fi\n- Wi-Fi name: PrintshopMini\n- Password: printshopmini\n- Type it exactly, with the same upper and lower case.\n💻 The store PCs have internet too.\n\n🏪 We don't run franchises yet. All PrintShop Mini stores are directly operated.\n\n📖 To see more\n[[go:faq.html#faq-28|Are stores open on long weekends and temporary holidays?]]\n[[go:faq.html#faq-61|Can I ask questions by phone?]]\n[[go:faq.html#faq-55|Can I bring pets or food into the store?]]\n[[go:faq.html#faq-62|Can I use Wi-Fi in the store?]]\n[[go:faq.html#faq-63|Can I open a franchise store?]]"}, "12": {"h": "n2ilo5", "q": "My print came out wrong. Can I get a refund?", "a": "📝 For a refund you must file a 'refund request'!\nWithout filing, there is no refund.\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n👇 Tap the picture below to open the refund request site.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-refund2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/refund|Go to refund request]]\n💻 There is also a [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop. You can file there too.\n\n✅ Refunded / handled\nMachine problems like printer breakdowns, paper jams, toner smudges and blank prints are handled by the store.\n(Blank prints only count when the printer machine is broken. Blank pages from user mistakes are not refunded.)\n\n❌ Hard to refund or reprint\n- It went wrong because you worked without reading the guide\n- It went wrong because you misunderstood the guide\n- Problems from PC crashes while using sites where you get a document after paying, sites with limited print counts, or government/financial sites (no compensation or refund)\n- The fee paid to issue a certificate when the PC crashed because you didn't choose [증명서전용PIN9999] (certificate printer) on TOEIC, school transcript/graduation certificate or Certpia sites (not refunded)\n- Content was cut off when printing (when you could have checked it in the preview)\n- You chose the Color printer but it printed in black and white (with the Color printer, the preview should be in color. You printed without changing options even though the preview was black and white, so you paid the color price but it printed in black and white)\n- You chose B&W, thought it would print in color because the preview was in color, and ask for a refund because it isn't in color\n- You printed a USB file without saving it to the PC, and it came out blank\n- You didn't save a compressed file to the PC, unzip it, and open the unzipped file by double-clicking before printing, so part or all came out blank\n- You didn't save a file from email · cloud · web drive to the PC and open the saved file by double-clicking before printing, so it came out wrong\n- The payment info screen showed B&W/color, two-sided/one-sided, paper size, pages and price before paying, but you paid without checking and then ask for a refund because it printed wrong\n\n⚠️ Always check the payment info screen before paying!\nThe payment info screen appears on the printer machine before the final payment. It shows:\n- B&W/color\n- Two-sided/one-sided\n- Paper size\n- Number of pages\n- Price\nIf you pay without checking and it prints, there is no refund.\n\n🤔 e.g.) You printed only 3 pages on the PC, but the printer machine asks for 2,500 won. 3 B&W pages can't cost that much.\n👉 If the pages or price are different from what you expect, don't pay."}, "54": {"h": "1wt9zf", "q": "When and how are refunds processed?", "a": "📝 Refunds are processed after you file a refund request and a manager checks it.\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n\n1. File it with the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop or on the refund request site.\n2. Write the last digits of your card, the amount, the time and the problem.\n3. Leave the problem print in the store when you file. (If you don't leave it, there is no refund)\n4. A manager checks what you filed.\n5. If a refund is possible, it's usually processed the next day. If card cancellation is hard, we refund to a bank account.\n\nℹ️ A manager tells you separately whether you'll get a refund, at the contact you gave.\n💡 If you have a reason you can't leave the print, ask a manager on Naver TalkTalk.\n\n💳 Toss kiosk payments are refunded like this.\n- They can't be cancelled electronically. We refund to a bank account.\n- When filing, choose [직접입력] (Enter directly) as the reason and enter the bank name, account number and account holder's name.\n- If you paid twice at the Toss kiosk by your own mistake, we send back the amount minus the fee. Never pay twice.\n- There are warnings posted on the Toss kiosk, so please read them.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-refund2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/refund|Go to refund request]]"}, "32": {"h": "124gtj7", "q": "I want to check the fax I sent.", "a": "📠 Look up sent faxes at '팩스확인' (Fax check).\n🔎 Enter the receiver's fax number.\n👇 Tap the picture to open the site.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-faxcheck2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/webfax|Check fax sending result]]\n💻 There is also a [팩스확인] (Fax check) icon on the store PC desktop. You can check there too.\n\n📝 Do this\n1. In [수신 번호] (Receiving number), enter the number of the place receiving the fax.\n2. Press [검색] (Search).\n3. In the table, check [전송 시간] (Send time), [전송 지점명] (Sending store), [수신 번호] (Receiving number), [페이지 수] (Pages), [전송 결과] (Result) and [수신 시간] (Received time).\n\n⏳ 1. Faxes may be slow\nIt's an internet fax, so it's slower than a phone-line fax.\nIt may take a while depending on the connection and the number of pages.\n👍 If you have many pages, send them 30 at a time!\n⚠️ If you send it again without waiting, you'll pay twice. Double payments are not refunded.\n\n🔍 2. Please wait even if nothing shows up at all\nIt's an internet fax, so lookups can be a bit slow.\nIf you enter the receiving number and nothing shows up\n1. ⏰ Look it up again after 5–10 minutes.\n2. ⛔ Don't send the fax again and pay twice just because it doesn't show up!\n3. 💬 Check with a manager first.\n   Send these 2 things on Naver TalkTalk.\n   - Store name\n   - Last 4 digits of the card you paid with\n4. ✅ A manager checks and tells you.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-fax.html#fax|How to check the fax sending result]]"}, "35": {"h": "1f3vdm4", "q": "The other person says they didn't receive my fax.", "a": "\"Didn't receive it\" can mean two things.\nFirst check the sending result on the fax check site. (See 'I want to check the fax I sent' above)\n\n❌ 1. It wasn't sent ([전송실패], Send failed)\nIf the fax check site says [전송실패] (Send failed), try in this order.\n\n🔢 ① First check again that the receiving fax number is correct.\n\n✅ ② If the number is correct\nIt may have failed because of a temporary connection problem.\n- Press [재전송] (Resend) on the fax check site.\n- ⚠️ You can resend only once.\n- Wait a moment, then check the sending result again.\n\n❌ ③ If it shows [전송실패] (Send failed) because the number was wrong\n👉 Please file a refund. We'll cancel the payment.\n\n⚠️ But if you typed the wrong number and that number is a working fax number, so it shows [전송완료] (Sent), we can't refund you.\n\n📄 2. They received a blank page, or the content was cut off\nThis happens when the original is put in the wrong way.\n\n📌 The ADF is the 'place to put originals' on top of the printer machine.\n[[sm:images/common/adf-feeder.jpg]]- They received a blank page\n  → The original had to go into the document feeder (ADF) with the content facing up, but it was put in with the content facing down.\n- The content was cut off\n  → The content was facing up, but the short edge of the original went to the left instead of the long edge.\n\n📝 Please file a refund first.\n- A manager checks it and tells you separately at the contact you gave whether you'll get a refund.\n- If the customer put the original in wrong, we can't refund. (Because the original has already become data and was sent to the fax server)\n\n⏰ You must file a refund within 7 days of the problem. If you don't file in time, we can't process the refund.\n\n👇 File a refund with the picture below.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-refund2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/refund|Go to refund request]]\n💻 You can also file with the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the store PC desktop.\n\n📖 Tap here for the picture guide.\n[[go:guide-fax.html#fax|How to send a fax]]"}, "28": {"h": "lcey4t", "q": "Are stores open on long weekends and temporary holidays?", "a": "✅ Yes, we're open 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, with no days off.\n\nEvery PrintShop Mini store is registered on Naver Smart Place.\n📍 Search on Naver to check the location, building name and floor before you visit."}, "55": {"h": "9gvg1k", "q": "Can I bring pets or food into the store?", "a": "❌ Pets are not allowed in the store.\n❌ Food is not allowed in the store either.\n\nPlease help keep it clean and safe. 🙏"}, "61": {"h": "1osr0op", "q": "Can I ask questions by phone?", "a": "📞 The phone number is posted all around the store. (PC desktop, monitors, etc.)\n🔎 Or search '프린트샵미니 + store name' on Naver to find the phone number.\n📞 But phone support is only on weekdays (Mon–Fri) 9 AM–9 PM.\n🚫 No phone support on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays.\n💬 At other times and on weekends/holidays, please contact us on Naver TalkTalk.\n\n📝 What to send on TalkTalk\n1. Store name\n2. The problem\n3. Contact number\n\n💡 The store name is written on the PC desktop or the sign next to the PC.\n💡 The phone number is posted in the store."}, "62": {"h": "ayqx8q", "q": "Can I use Wi-Fi in the store?", "a": "✅ Yes, you can use free Wi-Fi.\n\n📶 Wi-Fi name: PrintshopMini\n🔑 Password: printshopmini\n\n💡 Type it exactly, with the same upper and lower case.\n💻 The store PCs have internet too."}, "68": {"h": "17wcepw", "q": "I paid and it was printing fine, then it suddenly said \"no paper\" and stopped printing.", "a": "😮 Was it printing fine and then suddenly stopped saying \"no matching paper\"?\nThis happens because the PDF file has a page with a different size.\n\n🔎 Why does this happen?\n- It can happen even if the sizes in the machine's list all look right (A4·B4·A3).\n- Some page in the PDF may not be A4·B4·A3 size.\n  e.g.) In a 10-page PDF, one of pages 2–10 has a different size\n- When printing reaches that page, it says \"no matching paper\".\n- It's hard to know in advance. You only find out when you actually print.\n\n✅ How to prevent it (always do this before printing)\n1. Open the PDF files one at a time.\n2. In the print options, find 'PDF 페이지 크기에 따라 용지 소스 선택' (choose paper source by PDF page size).\n3. Be sure to uncheck that box.\n4. Send the print job again, starting from the part that didn't print.\n5. Go to the printer machine and pay.\n💡 When sending several files together, uncheck it in every PDF file.\n\n💸 Already paid and some parts didn't print?\n1. File a refund with the [환불신청] (Refund request) icon on the PC desktop.\n2. For the payment amount, write what you actually paid.\n3. For the refund amount, calculate and write the price of the parts that didn't print.\n⏰ You must file within 7 days of the problem. If you didn't file, or filed after 7 days, there is no refund.\nℹ️ Filing doesn't mean an instant refund. A manager checks it, processes only eligible cases, and tells you the result at the contact you gave.\n\n📖 Tap here for the PDF print settings pictures.\n[[go:guide-print.html#acrobat|See PDF print settings]]"}, "71": {"h": "177vrg8", "q": "How do I get the lost-and-found box password? (How to use the lost item check site)", "a": "🔑 You get the lost-and-found box password by text message at '분실물확인' (Lost item check).\n👇 Tap the picture below to open the lost item check site.\n[[btn:images/faq/btn-lostfound2.png|https://fax.printnuri.com/lostfound|Go to lost item check]]\n💻 You can also open it with the [분실물확인] (Lost item check) icon on the store PC desktop.\n\n⚠️ Please do it yourself. Managers won't tell you instead.\n💡 Only payments made within the last 30 days can be checked.\n💬 Text messages are sent at most 3 times a day. If you don't get one, check your spam folder too.\n\n📝 Do this\n1. Read the notice at the top and press [동의합니다] (I agree).\n   - Check and take only your own item, and put other items back in the box.\n   - When you're done, be sure to lock the box, check that it's locked, then leave.\n   - You may be responsible for problems caused by leaving the box open.\n2. In [지점명] (Store name), choose the store.\n3. Choose [분실하신 물건] (Lost item). (USB memory, credit/debit card, resident registration card, driver's license, passport, bankbook, other) For 'other', type it yourself.\n4. Enter [결제일자] (Payment date), [결제시간] (Payment time) and [결제 금액] (Payment amount). This is a payment you made at this store.\n5. Choose [카드 구분] (Card type).\n   - Samsung Pay · Apple Pay · kiosk payment (binding · laminating): enter the [승인번호(8자리)] (8-digit approval number).\n   - Credit card (physical card): enter the [앞 4자리] (first 4 digits) and [뒤 4자리] (last 4 digits) of the card number.\n6. Enter [연락처] (Contact number). Numbers only, without \"-\". (e.g. 01012345678)\n7. Press [비밀번호 요청] (Request password), and the box password is sent by text to the phone number you entered.\n\n🔎 Tap to see how to find the approval number.\n[[go:faq.html#faq-6|How to find the Samsung Pay · Apple Pay approval number]]\n\n⚠️ If you see these screens, do this\n- \"결제 정보를 찾을 수가 없습니다\" (Payment info not found): check the store, date, time, amount and card number (approval number) again.\n- \"문자 전송이 실패하였습니다\" (Text message failed): check your phone number again.\n- \"SMS 전송횟수를 초과하였습니다\" (SMS limit exceeded): you've gone over 3 times today. Check your phone's spam messages.\n\n📖 To learn what the lost-and-found box is and what to do if you lose an ID card or card, see the question below.\n[[go:faq.html#faq-29|I left my ID card, card or USB behind. Can you keep it for me?]]"}, "63": {"h": "17eu0n4", "q": "Can I open a franchise store?", "a": "We don't run a franchise business yet.\nAll PrintShop Mini stores now are directly operated. 🏪"}, "73": {"h": "1ekyuew", "q": "An Error window appears on the printer machine screen and it doesn't respond well.", "a": "This window appears if you hold the edge of the screen with your hand, or if something is placed on the screen.\n[[img:images/faq/touch-error.png]]\n⚠️ When this happens, the screen doesn't respond well.\n\nTry this.\n1. ✋ Take your hand off the edge of the screen.\n2. 📦 Remove anything placed on the screen (phone · wallet · paper).\n3. 👆 Tap buttons lightly with one finger.\n\n❌ Don't hold or lean on the screen!"}}, "cats": {"mini": {"name": "Mini programs", "desc": "Parking · receipts · refunds · fax check · lost items (how to use PrintShop Mini's own sites)"}, "broken": {"name": "Problems", "desc": "When the machine acts strange or a print comes out wrong"}, "use": {"name": "How to use", "desc": "When you want to know how to use something"}, "buy": {"name": "Products", "desc": "L-folders · document envelopes · slide-binder files"}, "store": {"name": "Store operation", "desc": "Hours · holidays · pets · phone · Wi-Fi · franchise"}, "pc": {"name": "PC programs", "desc": "When a program on the PC acts strange"}, "cmv3cynpb": {"name": "Lost items", "desc": "ID cards, cards, other items"}, "cmv3djben": {"name": "CCTV viewing", "desc": "Viewing CCTV, storing and sending footage"}}};
